            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0528" n="434" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124a/107b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-05T16:00:00-05:00">November 5, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>98. Department’s telegram No. 96, October 30, 1 p.m.<anchor n="12"
                        xml:id="d416-f1"/> Harvey Firestone Junior called at the Department today
                    and informed the Department that the Finance Corporation has decided to make the
                    advance of $11,000 requested by the Liberian Government for sanitation purposes.
                    Three thousand dollars will be made immediately available to the Fiscal
                    Agent.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
